  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# ControlNet, LoRA & Conditioning Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` simulates the two mechanisms on 1-D:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "1. **LoRA.** A pretrained linear layer `W`. Freeze it. Train a low-rank `B @ A` such that `W + BA` matches a target linear layer. Show that `r = 1` is enough to learn a rank-1 correction perfectly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "2. **ControlNet-lite.** A \"frozen base\" predictor and a \"side network\" that reads an extra signal. The side network's output is gated by a learnable scalar initialized to zero (our version of zero-conv). Train and watch the gate ramp up."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: LoRA math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def lora(W, A, B, x, alpha=1.0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # W is frozen; A, B are the trainable low-rank factors."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [W[i][j] * x[j] for i, j in ...] + alpha * (B @ (A @ x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: zero-init side network"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "side_out = control_net(x, condition)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "gated = gate * side_out  # gate initialized to 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "h = base(x) + gated"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "At step 0 the output is identical to base. Early training updates `gate` slowly \u2014 no catastrophic drift."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** In `code/main.py`, vary the LoRA rank `r` from 1 to 4. At what rank does the LoRA exactly match a rank-2 target delta?\n2. **Medium.** Train two separate LoRAs on two target transforms. Load them together and show their additive interaction. When does the interaction break linearity?\n3. **Hard.** Use diffusers to stack: SDXL-base + Canny-ControlNet (weight 0.8) + a style LoRA (\u03b1 0.8) + IP-Adapter (weight 0.6). Measure FID-vs-prompt-adherence trade-off as the stack weights vary."
      ]
    }
